      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.51,
      "end_seconds": 4.48,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Hi there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.1,
      "end_seconds": 10.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.24,
      "end_seconds": 18.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.87,
      "text": "Mainly chest tightness. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.27,
      "end_seconds": 27.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "alright, what's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.2,
      "end_seconds": 34.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Since Monday, that's when it began."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.92,
      "end_seconds": 40.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "I follow. Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.43,
      "end_seconds": 47.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "Mild, I'd say. I notice it it more with pollen season"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.41,
      "end_seconds": 68.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.06,
      "end_seconds": 79.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.63,
      "end_seconds": 106.74,
      "duration_seconds": 8.11,
      "text": "okay: temperature 36.5 respiratory rate 15. And SpO2 98 percent on room air pulse 82 pressure 108 over 75."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.41,
      "end_seconds": 108.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.93,
      "end_seconds": 112.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "that's fine I'll explain it soon"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.66,
      "end_seconds": 117.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "now I'm going to do a short physical check"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.07,
      "end_seconds": 122.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "fine by me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.54,
      "end_seconds": 125.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.12,
      "end_seconds": 142.48,
      "duration_seconds": 7.36,
      "text": "I can hear a faint wheeze at the end of breathing out, otherwise the chest is clear"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.74,
      "end_seconds": 147.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "You can relax now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.13,
      "end_seconds": 162.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "How about weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.13,
      "end_seconds": 166.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "No weight loss, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.13,
      "end_seconds": 173.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "A few quick ones: coughing up phlegm, chest pain or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.19,
      "end_seconds": 177.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "No, you know, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.76,
      "end_seconds": 182.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.83,
      "end_seconds": 185.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "nothing else aches"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.4,
      "end_seconds": 190.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.82,
      "end_seconds": 199.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.47,
      "text": "Asthma, for two years i thought it it would sort itself out, but it hasn't"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.07,
      "end_seconds": 216.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.71,
      "end_seconds": 220.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "no, I've never reacted to to anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.05,
      "end_seconds": 223.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "what's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.2,
      "end_seconds": 227.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.68,
      "end_seconds": 230.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.8,
      "end_seconds": 234.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "My partner and our baby"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.08,
      "end_seconds": 244.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "So do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.6,
      "end_seconds": 250.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "it's Seretide inhaler, twice a day for my asthma"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.45,
      "end_seconds": 265.53,
      "duration_seconds": 13.08,
      "text": "Putting it all together it fits best with exercise-triggered asthma with seasonal allergy. I want to be honest that this is an impression not a final answer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.63,
      "end_seconds": 269.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "is it dangerous, uh, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.53,
      "end_seconds": 287.56,
      "duration_seconds": 17.03,
      "text": "it's reasonable to be concerned but right now exercise-triggered asthma with seasonal allergy is my leading thought not anything worse. Stop me if I've got anything wrong. You've had chest tightness since Monday mild and no weight loss or coughing up phlegm"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.47,
      "end_seconds": 289.17,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.35,
      "end_seconds": 314.69,
      "duration_seconds": 24.34,
      "text": "I think a peak flow diary makes sense here, for asthma i want a breathing test done, that's for wheeze the result will help us decide whether anything more is needed for this, budesonide-formoterol inhaler, 200 micrograms, one puff twice a day, long term it's for asthma control rinse your mouth after the preventer inhaler and use the spacer"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.78,
      "end_seconds": 331.13,
      "duration_seconds": 15.35,
      "text": "one warning sign to remember: the inhaler isn't helping or you cannot speak in full sentences. In that case don't wait. See me again after the breathing test. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 335.53,
      "end_seconds": 337.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "thank you, doctor, goodbye"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.48,
      "end_seconds": 340.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "have a good day"
    }
  ]
